      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `python/sglang/srt/sampling/custom_logit_processor.py`, `ThinkingBudgetLogitProcessor.__call__` materializes `req.origin_input_ids + req.output_ids` on every decode step to locate `think_start_id` and count generated thinking tokens, and accepts `bool` values (`True`/`False`) for `thinking_budget` since `isinstance(True, int)` is `True` in Python.\n\n*(Note: rebased/updated after `#47196` landed the `DeepseekOCRNoRepeatNGramLogitProcessor` `window_size` tail slice on `main`.)*\n\n## Modifications\n\n- **`ThinkingBudgetLogitProcessor`**:\n  - Added `_open_thinking_tokens_after_start(origin_input_ids, output_ids)` to locate the last `think_start_id` across `output_ids` and `origin_input_ids` via reverse search without concatenating `origin_input_ids + output_ids`.\n  - Guarded `thinking_budget` validation with `not isinstance(thinking_budget, bool)` and guarded `req is None`.\n- **Unit Tests**:\n  - Added tests in `test/registered/unit/sampling/test_custom_logit_processor.py` covering `ThinkingBudgetLogitProcessor` across prompt and output boundaries and boolean `thinking_budget` rejection.\n\n## Accuracy & Benchmark Tests\n- `pytest test/registered/unit/sampling/test_custom_logit_processor.py -v` (`36 passed`)\n\nSigned-off-by: Parth Vadera <parthvadera@gmail.com>",
